label chapter_7_1:
    scene bg BATHROOM

    n "A childhood memory rose up slowly. When we were already 12, in-between Pomorimo Online sessions, Sharlene would always want me to come over to her house. When I got there it always felt a bit lowly. Her room was littered with all sorts of assorted garbage. Bits and pieces of anime merchandise that she wouldn’t bother to clean up, empty corn chip bags that she forgot about. At the time I didn’t think much of it, considering I wasn’t that ill-mannered of a child, but thinking back on it makes my stomach twist. It’s not a mystery figuring out why everybody at this damn school treats her the way they do. She’s an animal. She lives like one, she breathes like one, and she even proclaims to be one."

    nvl clear

    n "Whenever I go inside places, I make sure to always close the door behind me. The bathroom area door closed with a small click. A faint, disgusting ammonia smell hits my nose the moment I come in. It made me want to sneeze. I see her trying to find some sort of exit, staring at the windows frantically and turning her head around like some sort of idiot, and in her attempt to run back out past me, she trips. Her body foolishly drops to the floor. I hear her whine in pain. I didn’t do anything but watch her play out this idiot theater of hers. With the way she looked right now, Sharlene wasn’t any better than the roaches skittering around the floor. She tries to crawl around, feeling around for something. It’s probably that damned notebook again. I remember some of its contents and I remember I tried tearing up the cover once, because I wanted her to toss the thing out. She whined and cried every single time. It was something she’d do even up to now. It’s like she never grew out of being a child, like her body outgrew her before her mind."

    nvl clear

    n "I stomp at her ankle as she tries to reach for the thing. She yelps and tries to grab at my foot, but I kicked her other hand back."

    n "Fuck. You. You don’t deserve that notebook."

    n "You don’t deserve to be smirking like that."

    n "Fuck you. You don’t deserve anything."

    n "My foot swings back and forth at the creature on the floor. She started writhing like some kind of worm–no, maybe more like a fish out of water and she tried crying something out, but whatever it was, it was already useless. I couldn’t see her ribs under her uniform but I thought for sure that the skin might start bruising after I hit her hard enough a few times."

    nvl clear

    n "One. Two. I test a few kicks at the thing on the floor."

    n "She doesn’t even tell me to stop. Her pathetic hands keep clawing for the notebook. I kick it away, far under a bathroom stall. I see her make a grimace and it’s there I’m relieved she finally understands the gravity of the situation. All she can do is pathetically shield her face with her two lanky arms. I kick at her again. She chokes out a small yelp, but her grimace fades. She stares off to the side. I catch myself clicking my tongue in disgust–because she’s attempting to tap out again. I remind her with another swing of my foot and she barely reacts, only vaguely choking. I’m already tired of her. I’m tired of her useless existence, her useless games, her useless clamoring, her useless breaths."

    n "One. Two. Three. Four. Five. Each one is stronger than the last. She tries to grab at my foot again but it’s easy to shake off, considering how weak-willed she is right now."

    nvl clear

    n "Sharlene tries to crawl off into a stall, maybe to prevent me from damaging her already broken frame even further. She crawls towards the stall where her tattered notebook resides. I’m assuming it’s already soaked in leaking toilet water. I’m assuming she’s going to take it and hug it anyway, leafing through the pages like it’s the only thing she knows how to do. I pull on her uniform by the front. I want her to look at me directly. Her eyes don’t even shift to me when I do it. They’re focused entirely on the notebook."

    son "If not a siokoy, you have the brain of a dog, I swear…"

    son "Pay attention, dumbass."

    nvl clear

    n "All she does is whine sadly. She attempts to shake out of my grip but it’s so hapless, you can’t even consider this a fight. I snickered. She finally looks at me when she hears."

    n "Sharlene stares at me for a moment. Then two."

    n "Then her eyes widened."

    n "She thrashes around in my grip. She screams. Screams and screams and screams. She tries to bite down on my hand and it almost fucking hurts, but it makes me grip her uniform louder. She tries to push and smack me away from her face. It’s like she’s possessed. I keep her gripped and I could almost strangle her right now, but I don’t."

    shn "You’re not Sofia!!"

    shn "Who the fuck are you!? Get off! Get the fuck off!!"

    nvl clear

    son "What are you talking about?"

    n "She’s pissing me the fuck off. She’s annoying. Her voice is so shrill that my ears start ringing. She claws at me like a halfwit, and it’s there I’m convinced entirely that she’s just not human. And things that aren’t human, aren’t to be treated as human."

    n "I throw Sharlene down on the toilet seat. A little voice in my head recites a prayer, asking God to forgive me for what I’m about to do. I shifted my feet around, and while I did, I accidentally kicked the notebook into a puddle of water. I hear Sharlene howl. I kick her next."

    nvl clear

    n "My foot crushes the sides of her tattered face. It’s scarred with dots, acne, and old bruising. There’s faint streaks of red, obviously made with nails, and my shoe was planted firmly on every single one of those imperfections. I hoped that I could crush them out of her and do her a favor by making her face spotless. She cried out but she found it difficult to verbalize with a shoe in the way, and it only came out as strained, weak cries. I stomp. I stomp. I stomp again and again and again. I hoped she would fuck off and leave this Earth already. I hoped she would fuck off and dunk her head in the toilet water, swimming in shit like the siokoy she always claimed to be. "

    son "Fuck. You."

    nvl clear

    son "Shut up."

    son "Shut the hell up."

    nvl clear

    n "She tries to grab at my ankle but it’s useless. She can’t find the strength in her to move any more. Sharlene, in some sort of twisted acceptance, embraces every strike of my shoe to her face, her ribs, her gut. I see her shut her eyes tight, and I swear I could see her smiling at me again. She laughs. She laughs. But what comes out of her mouth sounds like a monster’s laugh. I don’t understand what she was finding so funny, but I found myself laughing, too. I painted more bruises under her shirt. I saw the purples and yellows clustering together as my shoe rubbed more grime on her uniform. When that got old, I started slapping her across the face too. She smiled at me every time she did. She was so happy. She was glad I was doing this for her. Every slap and smack of the face cleaned more grime off of her ugly mug. I hear her thanking me in between each slap. Of course, I beamed, because I was doing my friend a favor. I was finally helping get rid of her curse. I was going to beat it out of her and she was going to thank me. She was going to give me recompense for tearing my life away from me."

    nvl clear

    n "That’s right. I used to have a beautiful life. I used to live a life where I could go home and do ugly, boring things, and I used to have a life where I could go to school and ignore the rest of these pigs, focusing on making my mother happy. I used to have a beautiful life where Sharlene could do inefficient, inconvenient things, and nobody would have a problem with it, not even me. Everyone didn’t know of the siokoy’s existence yet. Everyone would live in idiot bliss and live happy lives not knowing anything about monsters and drowning and Sharlene’s idiocy. But then one day, the curse of the monster swallowed her whole. That’s why she acts like that. She made contact with a siokoy. It started turning her into one too. Now everybody’s afraid. Now that’s why I’m doing them a favor by defeating this fucking thing, so that everyone can be happy."

    nvl clear

    n "Everyone can go back to normal. Everyone can hold hands at school and act less like pigs. We’d all be joyous when the siokoy finally dies. And everything would return to the normal, boring state it was in. Even Sharlene would thank me for my heroic efforts. I would’ve triumphed and been given the highest honor, like in her stupid games. That’s why I’m sure she understands. She understands why this has to happen. She understands why I have to beat her until she’s bruised and black. In fact, she might be so mangled that it’s unrecognizable. It doesn’t give her any benefit to be recognizable anyway. At least this way nobody can see all the ugly parts of her face."

    nvl clear

    son "You understand, right?"

    son "You’re going to thank me."

    shn "......"

    n "My hands and legs stopped moving before I realized it. I was just in close contact with the monster now. Her temperature was hot, to such a suffocating degree. I’d assume it shot up because of some sort of adrenaline rush. A part of her face was flushed red."

    nvl clear

    n "Sharlene rubs at the bruises and winces hard when she does. I don’t know why she does it. She talks and I see she still has a full set of teeth. It’s a miracle she even does. I see her eyes drift to where the notebook was, and still, she picks it up. I don’t even know how much of that puddle was water and how much was piss."

    shn "… Are we playing later?"

    son "… Sorry?"

    shn "Are we playing later. Pomorimo."

    son "......"

    nvl clear

    son "I... I guess."

    n "Her hands wrap around my back. It’s awful. It’s so fucking awful because I feel the notebook sticking to my uniform. It’s still dripping wet. I didn’t give her permission to do that. For someone who might have the brain of a dog, she’s shit at acting like one."

    shn "You’re the best."

    shn "You really are."

    return
